# git-secrets false-positive allowlist (regexes matched per line).
#
# The `xai-[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+` pattern that catches real xAI API keys (which are
# literally prefixed `xai-`) also matches every ordinary hyphenated identifier
# starting with "xai": this repo's own `xai-voice` plugin name and directory
# path, xAI's package names, and the WebSocket subprotocol prefix.
#
# Each entry below is a specific known identifier, NOT a blanket `xai-.*`, so a
# real key still trips the hook. Tradeoff worth knowing: git-secrets exempts a
# whole LINE when any allowed pattern matches it, so a line that mentions one of
# these identifiers AND carries a real key would pass. These are package and
# path names, so that co-occurrence is not a realistic shape.
xai-voice
xai-sdk-python
xai-sdk-go
xai-proto
xai-org
xai-go
xai-client-secret
xai-grok-tts
xai-grok-voice
x-ai/grok-voice-tts
